<title>USA: First of America sets buyback program.</title>
<headline>First of America sets buyback program.</headline>
<dateline>KALAMAZOO, Mich. 1997-01-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>First of America Bank Corp said Friday its board authorized the repurchase of up to two million shares of common stock.</p>
<p>Shares repurchased will be used for general corporate purposes and may be available for reissuance in connection with compensation, dividend reinvestment and employee savings plans.</p>
<p>In 1996, the company completed a 3.6 million stock repurchase program. First of America's average number of outstanding shares in 1996 was 61.8 million.</p>
</text>
